WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.769
The owner asked to start, pause and
stop every service, and read its logs.

2
00:00:06.169 --> 00:00:07.483
None of that existed.

3
00:00:08.083 --> 00:00:13.975
So first, every service writes the same kind
of log, in rolling files tagged by app.

4
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:18.537
Then I added a small supervisor
that depends on none of the apps.

5
00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:22.984
It reports each service's
state, CPU, memory and uptime.

6
00:00:23.284 --> 00:00:26.665
It starts and stops them,
and streams their logs live.

7
00:00:26.965 --> 00:00:30.764
Because it stands apart, it still
answers when an app won't start.

8
00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:35.838
Pausing the workers is a row in the
database, not a signal or a file.

9
00:00:36.138 --> 00:00:40.809
Flip it, and the whole fleet pauses together,
while the study in flight finishes.

10
00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:44.937
An Operations page puts all
of it in one place, live.

11
00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:47.012
Then I cleaned up the cloud.

12
00:00:47.312 --> 00:00:51.449
Hosting and monitoring that had
never served a user were deleted.

13
00:00:51.849 --> 00:00:54.671
Deploys became one job, with a rollback.

14
00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:58.729
Push to live went from about fifteen
minutes to thirty-five seconds.
